### UNITAS -- API test template (VS Code REST Client extension)
### Fill in the variables below from web/.env.local, then click "Send Request"
### above any block. Reuses the same Supabase project as the root static
### site's coin-core wallet system -- these are the same wallets/spend_coins
### endpoints already live in production, so prefer a test/staging user
### token here rather than a real one when trying destructive calls.

@supabaseUrl = https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
@supabaseAnonKey = YOUR_ANON_KEY
@userAccessToken = YOUR_USER_JWT_FROM_SIGN_IN
@nextAppUrl = http://localhost:3000
@mockWebhookUrl = http://localhost:4242

### Supabase: current user's wallet balance
GET {{supabaseUrl}}/rest/v1/wallets?select=balance
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}

### Supabase: recent coin ledger entries
GET {{supabaseUrl}}/rest/v1/coin_ledger?select=amount,kind,module,created_at&order=created_at.desc&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}

### Supabase: spend_coins RPC (module access gate)
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/spend_coins
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "p_module": "Arche",
  "p_amount": 300
}

### Stripe webhook mock listener (root repo: `npm run mock:checkout`)
POST {{mockWebhookUrl}}/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "checkout.session.completed",
  "data": {
    "object": {
      "id": "cs_test_placeholder",
      "metadata": { "bundle": "small" }
    }
  }
}

